and equipment and intangible assets as key factors for free cash flow.

In addition, we continue to analyze and comment on sales at Group and segment level, but we do not
forecast them.

Calculation of EBITDA before special items

EBITDA is the result from income from operations reported in the Consolidated Financial Statements plus
depreciation, amortization, impairments and reversals of impairments on property, plant and equipment
and intangible assets. This is adjusted for</data>
