Price trends for key commodities

Due to increasing oil supply, weak overall growth in oil demand and OPEC’s announcement to increase
production, Brent North Sea crude prices fell from an average of $84 per barrel in the first half of 2024 to
$74 per barrel in the fourth quarter. The annual average oil price was $81 per barrel, only slightly below
the price of the previous year</data>
