of duties and dual control, or the “four-eyes principle.” Complex actuarial reports and evaluations are
produced by specialized service providers or specially qualified employees.

An internal control system for financial reporting continuously monitors these principles. To this end,
methods are provided to ensure that evaluation of the internal control system in financial reporting is
structured and uniform across the BASF G</data>
