      <data key="d2">118</data>
      <data key="d3">be made in writing or
through electronic communication outside of the meetings, as long as no Supervisory Board member
objects to this form of passing a resolution. The Supervisory Board meets regularly even without the
Board of Executive Directors.

The Board of Executive Directors continually informs the Supervisory Board about matters such as the
course of business and expected developments, the results of operations, net assets and financial
position, material acquisition and divestiture pro</data>
    </node>
