      <data key="d2">180</data>
      <data key="d3">icantly impact transportation, or even bring it to a standstill. We are currently working to more
precisely determine the scope of materiality of this risk and the sites affected. We have already taken
measures to counteract this risk (see page 224).

With respect to transition climate risks and opportunities, global climate policy ambitions and the
implementation of relevant measures play a decisive role in the continuing growth of the chemical
industry and its customer industries. Consequently</data>
