Resource inflows

E5-4

BASF’s most important raw materials (based on volume) include gas and crude oil-based petrochemical
feedstocks such as naphtha and benzene. We use liquid gas and natural gas as fuels to generate energy
and steam, and as raw materials to produce key basic chemicals such as ammonia or acetylene.
Naphtha is mainly fed into our steam crackers, where</data>
    </node>
