      <data key="d2">258</data>
      <data key="d3">At a Glance           Combined Management’s Report      Consolidated Financial Statements          Further Information

cogeneration of heat/cool and power from fossil gaseous fuels, reached the materiality threshold for the
first time in the 2024 business year in terms of their contribution to capital expenditures. The following
economic activities have been deemed immaterial: electricity generation using solar photovoltaic
technology; production of heat/cool from bioenergy; production of heat/</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BASF SE - 2024 - BASF Report (SustainabilityReports.com).pdf:page_258:chunk_2">
      <data key="d0">chunk</data>
      <data key="d1">BASF SE - 2024 - BASF Report (SustainabilityReports.com).pdf</data>
      <data key="d2">258</data>
      <data key="d3">We assessed the taxonomy eligibility of our sales revenue based on sales revenue as defined and
reported in the Consolidated Financial Statements of the BASF Group (see page 358). When taking all six
environmental objectives into account, our taxonomy-eligible sales revenue accounted for 11.7% of total
sales revenue in 2024. The largest contributions were from the activities manufacture of plastics in
primary form and manufacture of organic basic chemicals, both of which are assigned to the
envi</data>
    </node>
