– Plastics in primary form were analyzed with respect to the share of renewable raw materials in the
  product. They were only considered further if the share was at least 5% and thus potentially made a
   substantial contribution to climate change mitigation through partial or complete production from
  renewable raw materials. Shares allocated using mass balance approaches (s</data>
