      <data key="d3">1.7% of total operating expenditures, with the largest contribution coming from the
economic activity of manufacture of batteries (1.1%). There were no substantial changes to our
taxonomy-aligned sales revenues or capital and operating expenditures.

The taxonomy-aligned portion of BASF’s economic activities remains considerably lower than the
taxonomy-eligible portion due to various factors. For instance, only a small proportion of plastics in
primary form contain renewable raw materials in an </data>
