The HPI is based on various central assumptions, such as the recorded health data being representative
of the entire workforce. Participation in health programs is comprehensive but voluntary. A further
assumption is that the effects of the health programs on the well-being of employees are both
measurable and significant.

The index also has certain limitations which must be t</data>
