1.4  Accounting policies

The accounting policies for the individual items in the balance sheet and the income statement are
presented in the respective sections of the Notes.

Business combinations: In business combinations, the acquired assets and liabilities are recognized at
fair value on the date the acquirer effectively obtains control. The fair value of acquired asse</data>
