      <data key="d3">About This Report         Combined Management’s Report      Consolidated Financial Statements          Further Information

8  Functional costs

Under the cost of sales method, functional costs incurred by the operating functions are determined on
the basis of cost center accounting. The functional costs particularly contain the personnel costs,
depreciation and amortization accumulated on the underlying final cost centers as well as allocated costs
within the cost accounting cycle. Operating ex</data>
