22 Other provisions

Accounting policies

Other provisions are recognized when there is a present obligation as a result of a past event and when
there is a probable outflow of resources whose amount can be reliably estimated. Provisions are
recognized at the probable settlement value.

The probable amount required to settle noncurrent provisions is discounted if the effect</data>
