The fair value of a financial instrument is the price that would be received to sell an asset or paid to
transfer a liability in an orderly transaction between market participants at the measurement date. If
pricing on an active market is available, for example in the form of exchange prices, these are used as
the basis for the measurement. Otherwise, the measurement is bas</data>
    </node>
