      <data key="d2">415</data>
      <data key="d3">he hedges are
transferred from equity to the income statement in the reporting period in which the hedged item is
recognized in the income statement. The maturity of the hedging instrument is aligned with the effective
date of the future transaction.

When fair value hedge accounting is used, the asset or liability recognized is hedged against the risk of
a change in fair value. The hedging instruments used, which often take the form of a derivative, are
measured at fair value and changes in fai</data>
