25.2 Financial risks

Market risks

Foreign currency risks: Changes in exchange rates could lead to losses in the value of financial
instruments and adverse changes in future cash flows from planned transactions. Foreign currency risks
from financial instruments result from the translation at the closing rate of financial receivables, loans,
securities, cash and financial l</data>
