      <data key="d2">475</data>
      <data key="d3">S

Steam cracker

A steam cracker is a plant in which steam is used to “crack” naphtha (petroleum) or natural gas. The
resulting petrochemicals are the raw materials used to produce most of BASF’s products.

Substances of concern or very high concern

Substances of concern (SoC) are chemical substances which, if handled improperly, may have
potentially harmful effects on human health or the environment and which, based on their properties,
have a harmonized classification under the European CLP </data>
    </node>
