      <data key="d1">Eastman Chemical Co - 2025 - Annual Report (SustainabilityReports.com).pdf</data>
      <data key="d2">56</data>
      <data key="d3">Company utilizes currency-sensitive derivative instruments for hedging anticipated foreign
currency transactions, a loss in fair value from those instruments is generally offset by an increase in the value of the underlying anticipated transactions.

At December 31, 2025, a 10 percent fluctuation in the euro and Japanese yen currency rates would have had an impact of $259 million and $5 million,
respectively, on the designated net investment values in the foreign subsidiaries. As a result of the</data>
    </node>
