      <data key="d3">ders. The majority of the Company's terms of sale have a single performance obligation to transfer products. Accordingly, the
Company recognizes revenue when control has been transferred to the customer, generally at the time of shipment of products.

Eastman accounts for shipping and handling as activities to fulfill the promise to transfer the good and does not allocate revenue to those activities. All
related shipping and handling costs are recognized at the time of shipment. Amounts collecte</data>
    </node>
