      <data key="d3">ciated costs are removed from the appropriate property accounts.

For additional information, see Note 4, "Properties and Accumulated Depreciation" and Note 16, "Asset Impairments, Restructuring, and Other Charges,
Net".
Depreciation and Amortization

Depreciation expense is calculated based on historical cost and the estimated useful lives of the assets, generally using the straight-line
method. Estimated useful lives for buildings and building equipment generally range from 20 to 50 years. Est</data>
    </node>
