Goodwill

Goodwill is an asset determined as the residual of the purchase price over the fair value of identified assets and liabilities
acquired in a business combination. Eastman conducts testing of goodwill for impairment annually in the fourth quarter or more frequently when events
and circumstances indicate an impairment may have occurred. The testing of goodwill is performed at the "reporting unit" level which the Company has
determin</data>
    </node>
