      <data key="d3">tive
analysis in testing the carrying value of goodwill of each reporting unit for impairment. When the quantitative analysis is used, the Company uses an
income approach, specifically a discounted cash flow model.

Indefinite-lived Intangible Assets

Eastman conducts testing of indefinite-lived intangible assets annually in the fourth quarter or more frequently when events and circumstances indicate
an impairment may have occurred. The carrying value of an indefinite-lived intangible asset is c</data>
    </node>
